The events were separated into four separate centrality bins: peripheral events which represent 50% to 70% centrality, semi-peripheral events which represent 30% to 50% centrality, semi-central events which represent 10% to 30% centrality, and central events which represent the top 10% central events. The most peripheral bin (70% to 100% centrality) was not used in this analysis due to the low overall event multiplicity which made extracting meaningful physics virtually impossible, and because there was a strong trigger bias for events in this centrality range.

